<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1"><ac:rich-text-body><p>This page has been generated with a tool.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h1>Purpose</h1><p>This Model Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) Work Instruction demonstrates the procedures to create structural diagrams in the Problem Domain. Adherence to this document ensures that new SysML diagrams conform to DRS Naval Electronics process and quality standards.</p><h1>DRS Naval Electronics SysML Meta Model</h1><p>This Work Instruction addresses the <strong>Problem Domain Black Box - Structure</strong> space of the DRS Naval Electronics Meta Model; see <a href="#fig-drsne-meta-model">Figure 1</a>.</p><p>In the Problem Domain, the SoI is modeled as a <em>black box</em>; only the external boundaries and connections are defined. The black box perspective helps the modeler identify the most fundamental SoI specifications: external interfaces, and the states, behaviors, and functions inferred from its inputs and outputs. Allocating these specifications to discrete objects within the SoI gives rise to structure in the system model.</p><hr/><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">fig-drsne-meta-model</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><p><ac:image ac:align="center"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PDSCDiagramsMetaModel.png"/></ac:image></p><hr/><h1>Procedure</h1><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="toc"><ac:parameter ac:name="minLevel">2</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="maxLevel">7</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="type">list</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="outline">true</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><h2>Create Elements of Definition</h2><p>Create elements by right-clicking in the containment tree.</p><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:rich-text-body><p>Customizations are located under <strong>Other Blocks</strong>; see <a href="#fig-element-customizations">Figure 2</a>.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><hr/><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">fig-element-customizations</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><p><ac:image ac:align="center"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PDSCcustomizations.png"/></ac:image></p><hr/><h3>Create Problem Domain System Context Block</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Right-click <strong>System Context (Structure) &gt; Create Element &gt; Domain</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Open the element <strong>Specification</strong> and edit the <strong>Documentation</strong>. Write a brief description of the PDSC.</p></li></ol><h3>Create System of Interest</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Right-click <strong>System Context (Structure) &gt; Create Element &gt; System of Interest</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="System of Interest"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_systemofinterest.png"/></ac:image>.</p></li><li><p>Open the element <strong>Specification</strong> and edit the <strong>Documentation</strong>. Write a brief description of the SoI.</p></li></ol><h3>Create Actors</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Right-click <strong>Actors &gt; Create Element &gt; Actor</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="actor"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_actor.png"/></ac:image>.</p></li><li><p>Open the actor <strong>Specification</strong> and edit the <strong>Documentation</strong>. Write a brief description of each element.</p></li><li><p>Open the <strong>Actor Descriptions</strong> table and drag all actors into the table.</p></li><li><p>In the top toolbar, select <strong>Columns &gt; Documentation</strong>. A new column displaying the <strong>Documentation</strong> field is added to the table.</p></li></ol><h3>Create External Systems</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Under <strong>Structure</strong>, right-click <strong>External Systems &gt; Create Element &gt; External System</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="anchor"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_externalsystem.png"/></ac:image>.</p></li><li><p>Open the External System <strong>Specification</strong> and edit the <strong>Documentation</strong>. Write a brief description of each element.</p></li><li><p>Open the <strong>External System Descriptions</strong> table and drag all external systems into the table.</p></li><li><p>In the top toolbar, select <strong>Columns &gt; Documentation</strong>. A new column displaying the <strong>Documentation</strong> field is added to the table.</p></li></ol><hr/><h2>Create Block Definition Diagram</h2><p>Add elements to diagrams by dragging them from the containment tree. Create relationships by drawing connections in the diagram.</p><p>Right-click the <strong>PDSC block</strong> <strong>&gt; Create Diagram &gt; SysML Block Definition Diagram</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="block definition diagram"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_bdd.png"/></ac:image>, and enter {{[project/system name] Problem Domain System Context}}. </p><h3>Layout the Diagram</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Drag the PDSC block into the middle of the diagram and lengthen it to extend to the bottom of the screen.</p></li><li><p>Update the title to match the element name.</p></li><li><p>Drag the SoI block onto the diagram above the PDSC block, all actors to the left, and all external systems to the right.</p></li><li><p>Drag the <strong>Actor Descriptions</strong> table into the top-left region and  the <strong>External System Descriptions</strong> table into the top-right region.</p></li><li><p>Use the <strong>Align</strong> tool <ac:image ac:alt="Align"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_align.png"/></ac:image> in the top toolbar to organize, resize, and reposition elements to give the diagram a uniform style.</p></li></ol><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:rich-text-body><p>All external system and actor blocks should be roughly the same size.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><h3>Create Design Comments</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Select the element to attach a comment to, then select the anchor <ac:image ac:alt="anchor"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_Anchor.png"/></ac:image>. Move the mouse to nearby whitespace and click to create a note.</p></li><li><p>Right-click the note, then <strong>Refactor &gt; Convert To &gt; Comment</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Right-click again, and under <strong>Stereotype</strong>, select a comment stereotype.</p></li><li><p>Enter the comment in the text field.</p></li></ol><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:rich-text-body><p>All design comments should have an applied stereotype.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><h3>Create System of Interest Documentation Comment</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Right-click the SoI <strong>&gt; Specification</strong>. Expand the <strong>Documentation/Comments</strong> category in the left navigation menu.</p></li><li><p>Click and drag the comment nested under <strong>Documentation/Comments</strong> into the top-left region to create a <strong>Comment</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Mouse over the comment and select the anchor <ac:image ac:alt="anchor"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_Anchor.png"/></ac:image>, then select the PDSC block and connect the elements.</p></li></ol><hr/><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">fig-display-soi-documentation</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><p><ac:image ac:align="center"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PDSCSOIContainmentTree.png"/></ac:image></p><hr/><h3>Create Relationships</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Create <strong>Directed Aggregation</strong> relationships from the PDSC block to each of the actors and external systems.</p></li><li><p>Create a <strong>Directed Composition</strong> relationship from the PDSC block to the SoI block.</p></li><li><p>Right-click each new connector <strong>&gt; Specification &gt; Multiplicity</strong>, and set the correct value.</p></li></ol><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:rich-text-body><p>The primary user should be assigned a multiciplity of <strong>[1..*]</strong></p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><h3>Output</h3><p><a href="#fig-pdsc-bdd">Figure 4</a> provides an example of a properly styled PDSC BDD.</p><hr/><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">fig-pdsc-bdd</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><p><ac:image ac:align="center"><ri:attachment ri:filename="bigdia1.png"/></ac:image></p><hr/><h2>Create Internal Block Diagram</h2><p>Add elements to diagrams by dragging them from the containment tree. Create relationships by drawing connections in the diagram.  </p><p>In the containment tree, right-click the PDSC block <strong>&gt; Create Diagram &gt; SysML Internal Block Diagram</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="internal block diagram"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_ibd.png"/></ac:image> <strong>&gt; OK</strong>. Cameo automatically adds all elements of definition to the new diagram.</p><h3>Layout the Diagram</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Drag the SoI block into the middle of the diagram and lengthen it to extend to the bottom of the screen.</p></li><li><p>Update the title in the text box so it matches the file name.</p></li><li><p>Drag all actors to the left and all external systems to the right.</p></li><li><p>Drag the <strong>Actor Descriptions</strong> table into the top-left region and the <strong>External System Descriptions</strong> table into the top-right region.</p></li><li><p>Use the <strong>Align</strong> tool <ac:image ac:alt="Align"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_align.png"/></ac:image> in the top toolbar to organize, resize, and reposition elements to give the diagram a uniform style.</p></li><li><p>Drag the <strong>Interface Types</strong> legend into the top-left region.</p></li></ol><h3>Create Connections and Ports</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Select a property (element) in the diagram, then select the <strong>Proxy Port</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="Port"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_Port.png"/></ac:image>. Create a new port on the inner side (close to the SoI).</p></li><li><p>Select the SoI and create another port that will connect the SoI with the property port.</p></li><li><p>Select each port on the SoI, select the <strong>Connector</strong> <ac:image ac:alt="Connector"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PAR_assets_MBSE_Connector.png"/></ac:image>, then create a connection between the SoI and property ports.</p></li><li><p>Right-click each port <strong>&gt; Legend Item</strong>, then assign the appropriate <strong>Legend Item</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Position all port labels next to their ports and inside the owning block.</p></li></ol><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:rich-text-body><p>Connected ports should be horizontally aligned to the greatest possible extent. Use the <strong>Align</strong> tool.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><hr/><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">fig-port-style</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><p><ac:image ac:align="center"><ri:attachment ri:filename="PDSCPortStyle.png"/></ac:image></p><hr/><h3>Create Flows and Interfaces</h3><ol start="1"><li><p>Identify and create elements to represent all types of information flowing between the SoI and external systems.</p></li><li><p>Right-click <strong>Logical Information Flows &gt; Create Element &gt; Flow Specification</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Drag the Flow Specification block onto the appropriate connector in the diagram.</p></li><li><p>Check the flow's direction to confirm it is correct, then select <strong>Finish</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Identify all types of interfaces through which information is transferred between all PDSC elements of definition.</p></li><li><p>Right-click <strong>Logical Interface Types &gt; Create Element &gt; Interface Block</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Drag the Interface Block onto the appropriate port in the diagram.</p></li></ol><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="note"><ac:rich-text-body><p>All connected ports must be typed by the same Interface Block.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><p>The resulting IBD should look similar to <a href="#fig-pdsc-ibd">Figure 6</a>.</p><hr/><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">fig-pdsc-ibd</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><p><ac:image ac:align="center"><ri:attachment ri:filename="bigdia2.png"/></ac:image></p><hr/><h1>Revision History</h1><table data-layout="default"><thead><tr><th><p>Version</p></th><th><p>Revision</p></th><th><p>Date</p></th><th><p>Author</p></th><th><p>Change History</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>conf.1</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>03-02-2026</p></td><td><p>D. Ricart</p></td><td><p>Draft uploaded to General Engineering Practices Confluence space.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>References</h1><p>The Modeler should review <a href="#tab-work-instruction-inputs">Table 1</a> to ensure they have the required process inputs for the work activities described in this MBSE Work Instruction.</p><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">tab-work-instruction-inputs</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><table data-layout="default"><thead><tr><th><p>Document</p></th><th><p>Description</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>MBSE-WI-001 Teamwork Cloud Administrator</p></td><td><p>The Modeler should have access to the required work elements in Teamwork Cloud.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>MBSE-WI-002 Project Templates</p></td><td><p>The Modeler should be working in a Model using the DRS Naval Electronics MBSE package framework.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>Roles and Responsibilities</h1><p>Roles and responsibilities for the MBSE Style Guide are assigned with a RACI chart. Roles are defined in <a href="#tab-raci-roles-definitions">Table 2</a> and functional areas are assigned roles in <a href="#tab-pdsc-raci-chart">Table 3</a>.</p><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">tab-raci-roles-definitions</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><table data-layout="default"><thead><tr><th><p>RACI Role</p></th><th><p>Definition</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>Responsible</p></td><td><p>Stakeholder is the owner of the document.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Accountable</p></td><td><p>Stakeholder depends on the document to effectively perform their job duties.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Consulted</p></td><td><p>Stakeholder provides input, which may or may not be optional, to the authoring of the document.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Informed</p></td><td><p>Stakeholder is made aware of the document.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Omitted</p></td><td><p>Not a stakeholder.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="anchor"><ac:parameter ac:name="">tab-pdsc-raci-chart</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p><table data-layout="default"><thead><tr><th><p>Function</p></th><th><p>Role</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>Systems Engineering</p></td><td><p>R</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Project Engineering</p></td><td><p>C</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Configuration Management</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Electrical Engineering</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Mechanical Engineering</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Software Engineering</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Test Engineering</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Manufacturing</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Specialty Engineering</p></td><td><p>I</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Quality</p></td><td><p>A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Training</p></td><td><p>A</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Business Development</p></td><td><p>A</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>Terms</h1><table data-layout="default"><thead><tr><th><p>Term</p></th><th><p>Definition</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>Problem Domain System Context</p></td><td><p>the environment containing and surrounding the system of interest during key activities.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>System of Interest</p></td><td><p>the primary subject of the modeler's efforts, the system to be designed using the architectural definition realized in the system model.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Project Usage</p></td><td><p>a reference to a different project that provides access to that project's model elements</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Category</p></td><td><p>synonymous with <em>folder</em> in Teamwork Cloud</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Resource</p></td><td><p>synonymous with <em>file</em> in Teamwork Cloud</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Containment Tree</p></td><td><p>synonymous with <em>file directory</em> in Teamwork Cloud</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h1>Appendix</h1><h2>Actors Supplement</h2><p>Actors represent humans or human groups who interact with the SoI in the Problem Domain System Context. A common approach to designating actors is to consider them in terms of their <em>behaviors</em> and <em>needs</em> and how these characteristics may influence and/or interact with the SoI.</p><h2>External Systems Supplement</h2><p>External Systems are the systems that interact with the SoI in the Problem Domain. Common examples include power, networking, and thermal control systems, and structural systems such as mounts and cable harnesses. Identifying all external systems is critical to the definition of the SoI from a black box perspective.</p>